*> The combat rules wired into the play path (docs/protocol/17 sections 4.1 to 4.7 and 5.1; US14): the Attack packet with a standard-set tool, the hurt
*> pipeline of a player victim (hurt window, armor, toughness, Resistance, Protection) and the durability of the weapon and of the worn armor. The
*> formulas are the programs of tools-combat.cob, tools-armor.cob and tools-durability.cob; the enchantment numbers are parsed from the registry rows
*> (ench-load.cob).
*>   COMBAT-ENCHANT-SUM USING item stack handle, component key (PIC X(48)), ENCH-CTX, start (ten-thousandths), result out: folds the component over
*>     every enchantment of the stack (each level above 0 of the enchantment registry)
*>   COMBAT-ARMOR-STATS USING player row, ENCH-CTX, armor out (points), toughness out (thousandths), knockback resistance out (thousandths),
*>     protection out (ten-thousandths of points): the worn armor of the row (MN-EQUIP slots 1 to 4)
*>   COMBAT-EQUIP-HURT USING player row, equipment slot 1 to 4, amount: hurtAndBreak of a worn armor piece (Unbreaking, break at max_damage),
*>     Container Set Slot of the container slot (8 - slot + ... : boots 8, leggings 7, chestplate 6, helmet 5)
*>   HEALTH-HURT USING player row, amount (thousandths), cause (RULES.cpy CAUSE-*), source entity id (0 none), attacker player row (0 none), result out
*>     (0 ignored, 1 a fresh hit, 2 only the excess over lastHurt): the damage rules of 4.4 and 4.7 in thousandths of a point (HEALTH-DAMAGE is
*>     this program over whole points). Armor, Resistance and Protection apply to CAUSE-PLAYER; the other causes bypass armor (17 section 4.12)
*>   COMBAT-ATTACK USING attacker player row, target entity row: the attack of 4.2 for the standard set: the attack strength scale, the base
*>     damage of the held item, the damage enchantments, critical hit, hurt of a player target (or HEALTH-MOB-DAMAGE for any other entity row),
*>     knockback, and the durability of the held tool. Called by HEALTH-ATTACK when the open content set is not the cobolcraft set
*>   COMBAT-TICKER-RESET USING player row: the attack strength ticker restarts (a changed held slot)

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. COMBAT-TICKER-RESET.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY CTOOLS.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-ROW                  BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ROW.
     MOVE PL-ENTITY-ID(L-ROW) TO TS-OWNER(L-ROW)
     COMPUTE TS-LAST-ATTACK(L-ROW) = CW-TICKS + 1
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM COMBAT-TICKER-RESET.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. COMBAT-ENCHANT-SUM.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CONTENT.
 01 WS-REGISTRY            PIC X(112) VALUE "enchantment".
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEVEL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NEXT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOLD-STATUS         BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY ENCHCTX REPLACING LEADING ==EC-== BY ==LC-==.
 01 L-HANDLE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-COMPONENT            PIC X(48).
 01 L-START                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-RESULT               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-HANDLE L-COMPONENT ENCH-CTX L-START L-RESULT.
     MOVE L-START TO L-RESULT
     IF L-HANDLE = 0
         GOBACK
     END-IF
     CALL "CONTENT-REGISTRY-COUNT" USING WS-REGISTRY WS-COUNT WS-STATUS
     MOVE L-START TO WS-VALUE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-ID FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-ID >= WS-COUNT
         CALL "SP-ENCHANT-LEVEL" USING L-HANDLE WS-ID WS-LEVEL
         IF WS-LEVEL > 0
             CALL "ENCH-FOLD" USING WS-ID L-COMPONENT WS-LEVEL ENCH-CTX WS-VALUE WS-NEXT WS-FOLD-STATUS
             MOVE WS-NEXT TO WS-VALUE
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE WS-VALUE TO L-RESULT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM COMBAT-ENCHANT-SUM.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. COMBAT-ARMOR-STATS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY CMENU.
 COPY CITEMS.
 01 WS-WORN.
    05 WS-WORN-KEY         PIC X(48) OCCURS 5 TIMES.
 01 WS-SLOT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ITEM                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TENTHS-T            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TENTHS-K            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COMPONENT           PIC X(48) VALUE "minecraft:damage_protection".
 01 WS-NEXT                BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY ENCHCTX REPLACING LEADING ==EC-== BY ==LC-==.
 01 L-ROW                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-ARMOR                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-TOUGHNESS            BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-KNOCKBACK            BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-PROTECTION           BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ROW ENCH-CTX L-ARMOR L-TOUGHNESS L-KNOCKBACK L-PROTECTION.
     MOVE 0 TO L-ARMOR L-TOUGHNESS L-KNOCKBACK L-PROTECTION
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-WORN
     PERFORM VARYING WS-SLOT FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-SLOT > 4
         MOVE MN-EQUIP-ITEM(L-ROW, WS-SLOT) TO WS-ITEM
         IF MN-EQUIP-COUNT(L-ROW, WS-SLOT) > 0 AND WS-ITEM > 0 AND WS-ITEM < IT-COUNT
             MOVE IT-KEY(WS-ITEM + 1) TO WS-WORN-KEY(WS-SLOT)
             CALL "COMBAT-ENCHANT-SUM" USING MN-EQUIP-VAR(L-ROW, WS-SLOT) WS-COMPONENT ENCH-CTX L-PROTECTION WS-NEXT
             MOVE WS-NEXT TO L-PROTECTION
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "TOOL-ARMOR-TOTAL" USING WS-WORN L-ARMOR WS-TENTHS-T WS-TENTHS-K
     COMPUTE L-TOUGHNESS = WS-TENTHS-T * 100
     COMPUTE L-KNOCKBACK = WS-TENTHS-K * 100
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM COMBAT-ARMOR-STATS.

